INT. COMMUNITY CENTER BASEMENT, BINGO NIGHT - NIGHT

Folding tables, fluorescent flicker, a coffee urn the size of a toddler. Forty chairs, eleven players. A cage of numbered balls spins slowly.

Behind the microphone, MARGUERITE "MAGS" DELACOURT-PIKE (60s, cardigan, rhinestone glasses) holds a ball. At table three, DARNELL FONTAINE (30s, delivery uniform) hunches over four cards. Beside him, his mother LORRAINE FONTAINE (60s, church hat) marks each number with a stub of crayon.

MAGS
B-nine.

LORRAINE
That's yours.

DARNELL
I know it's mine.

MAGS
I-twenty-two.

DARNELL
Mama, I told you I'd come on Thursday.

LORRAINE
You said Thursday, and then you said Friday, and then you said next week.

MAGS
N-forty-one.

DARNELL
I've been working doubles.

LORRAINE
Doing what?

DARNELL
Deliveries. The same as last time you asked.

MAGS
G-fifty-six.

LORRAINE
(marking)
Funny. I called the depot. They said you quit in May.

Darnell's crayon stops. He puts it down.

DARNELL
You called my work.

LORRAINE
I called a number on your jacket.

MAGS
O-seventy-one.

A STRANGER (40s, windbreaker, clipboard) sits at the edge of table three. Nobody saw him arrive.

STRANGER
Mr. Fontaine. I'm sorry to interrupt.

DARNELL
Who are you?

STRANGER
Calvin Ortega, county clerk's office. You missed three hearings.

LORRAINE
What hearings?

DARNELL
Mama, don't.

CALVIN
I only need a signature, sir. Right here.

MAGS
Table three, keep it down, please. B-four.

Darnell takes the pen. Signs. His hand shakes. Lorraine reads the form over his shoulder, then looks at the cards, then at him.

LORRAINE
You lost the apartment.

DARNELL
In June.

LORRAINE
Where have you been sleeping?

DARNELL
In the van. Until they took the van.

MAGS
B-nine. Again. Somebody's got a B-nine.

Lorraine stands. The chair scrapes. Heads turn. She takes off her church hat and puts it down on the table, very gently, like laying a flag.

LORRAINE
You come home. Tonight.

DARNELL
Mama--

LORRAINE
I am not asking.

DARNELL
(rising, voice cracking)
Why are you doing this here? In front of everyone?

LORRAINE
Because everywhere else you stop picking up the phone.

He flings the cards. They scatter. Marked or not, they rain across the floor.

DARNELL
I didn't want you to see me like this!

MAGS
Table three!

DARNELL
Like what? Like a man who failed?

Calvin retreats three steps, clipboard raised like a shield. Mags has gone silent, one ball in her fist. Eleven players watch. The cage creaks once more and stops.

LORRAINE
Like my son.

He stands there. She does not move. Mags, very softly, into the microphone.

MAGS
Bingo, I think. If anyone's asking.
